<div class="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100">
  <.marketing_nav current_user={@current_user} current={:docs} />

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <.docs_layout
      current="billing"
      updated="August 23, 2026"
      toc={[
        {"plans", "Plans and limits"},
        {"entitlements", "What each plan unlocks"},
        {"usage-and-limits", "When you reach a limit"},
        {"changing-plan", "Upgrading and downgrading"},
        {"invoices", "Invoices and payment method"},
        {"payment-failure", "If a payment fails"},
        {"retention", "Plan changes and audit retention"}
      ]}
    >
      <.docs_header current="billing">
        <:dek>
          Your plan sets this account's runner capacity, included users, audit retention, and
          available features. Billing runs on Paddle; manage it on the
          <a
            href={~p"/app/billing"}
            class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
          >Billing</a>
          page in the console.
        </:dek>
      </.docs_header>

      <.docs_h2 id="plans">Plans and limits</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        emisar has three plans; a new account starts on Free.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-zinc-900">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[520px] text-left text-sm">
          <thead class="border-b border-zinc-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Plan</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Runners</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Team members</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Audit retention</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-zinc-900 text-zinc-400">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">Free</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">3</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">1</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">7 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">Team</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">100</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">Unlimited</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">90 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">Enterprise</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">Unlimited</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">Unlimited</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">365 days</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Free does not require a credit card and has no time limit. Team is billed per enabled runner, monthly
        or annually — annual costs about two months less, and checkout uses your current
        enabled-runner count (minimum one). Enterprise is a custom, sales-led plan with
        tailored limits. For the current per-runner price, <.link
          href={~p"/pricing" <> "#compare"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >compare the plans</.link>.
      </p>

      <.docs_h2 id="entitlements">What each plan unlocks</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Free includes the console, audit trail, policies, approvals, and runbooks; paid plans
        add the features below.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-zinc-900">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[520px] text-left text-sm">
          <thead class="border-b border-zinc-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Feature</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Available on</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-zinc-900 text-zinc-400">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">Single sign-on (OIDC)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top whitespace-nowrap">Team and Enterprise</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">Audit export (CSV + SIEM)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top whitespace-nowrap">Team and Enterprise</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top text-zinc-300">SCIM directory sync</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top whitespace-nowrap">Enterprise</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="flex-none text-zinc-500">—</span>
          <span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Single sign-on.</strong>
            OIDC sign-in through your identity provider. See <.link
              navigate={~p"/docs/sso"}
              class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
            >single sign-on &amp; SCIM</.link>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="flex-none text-zinc-500">—</span>
          <span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Audit export.</strong>
            Every plan keeps the full trail in the console; taking it out — the CSV download
            and the NDJSON API — is what the plan gates. See <.link
              navigate={~p"/docs/audit-and-siem"}
              class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
            >audit &amp; SIEM</.link>.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="flex-none text-zinc-500">—</span>
          <span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">SCIM directory sync.</strong>
            Provision and deprovision members from your directory. Enterprise also includes a
            security and procurement review, deployment planning, and rollout support from our
            team.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <.docs_h2 id="usage-and-limits">When you reach a limit</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Runner caps are enforced when you add the next one, not retroactively — a plan never
        silently disables a runner you already have. The Billing page shows live runner and
        member usage.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="flex-none text-zinc-500">—</span>
          <span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Runners.</strong>
            Enrolling a runner past the cap is refused — the registration fails with an
            over-limit error, and existing runners keep working.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="flex-none text-zinc-500">—</span>
          <span>
            <strong class="text-zinc-200">Audit retention</strong>
            is a time window, not a cap — plan changes and pruning are covered <.link
              href="#retention"
              class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
            >below</.link>.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <.docs_h2 id="changing-plan">Upgrading and downgrading</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Anyone in the account can open
        <a
          href={~p"/app/billing"}
          class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >Billing</a>
        and read the plan, its limits, and how much of them is in use. Changing the plan,
        updating the card, and cancelling take an owner, admin, or billing manager — a role
        owners and admins can grant to the person who owns invoices but not infrastructure.
        For the list of roles and permissions, see <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/teams-and-access"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >Teams &amp; access</.link>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        To upgrade, open <a
          href={~p"/app/billing"}
          class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >Settings → Billing</a>, pick <strong class="text-zinc-200">Monthly</strong>
        or <strong class="text-zinc-200">Annual</strong>, choose a plan, and pay in the
        Paddle checkout that opens on the page. The new plan and its limits take effect once
        Paddle confirms the charge.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        To downgrade or cancel, open
        <a
          href={~p"/app/billing"}
          class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >Settings → Billing</a>
        and choose <strong class="text-zinc-200">Manage subscription</strong>
        — it opens the Paddle customer portal. Do not start another checkout for this change.
      </p>
      <.docs_callout kind={:note} title="Cancelling keeps your plan until the period ends">
        <p>
          Cancelling does not cut access immediately: the plan and its limits stay active
          until the cancellation date Paddle schedules, and Billing shows that date. At that
          deadline the account moves to Free limits. Paid integrations become dormant, but their
          configuration is kept so an owner can resubscribe or clean up.
        </p>
      </.docs_callout>
      <.docs_callout kind={:note} title="Payment recovery keeps Team access available">
        <p>
          When an automatic payment is past due, Paddle manages the retry period and Team features
          remain available. If recovery ends in a pause or cancellation, the account moves to Free
          limits. Billing shows the current state and links to payment details.
        </p>
      </.docs_callout>

      <.docs_h2 id="invoices">Invoices and payment method</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        The Billing page shows recent invoices — date, amount, number, and status — each
        with a PDF download.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Open the Paddle customer portal for full invoice history, payment methods, billing
        addresses, and tax details. Start from
        <a
          href={~p"/app/billing"}
          class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >Settings → Billing</a>
        and choose <strong class="text-zinc-200">Manage subscription</strong>. Paddle is
        emisar's merchant of record and holds the complete ledger and card details — it is
        PCI DSS compliant and SOC 2 Type II audited (see <a
          href="https://trust.paddle.com/"
          class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >Paddle's trust center</a>).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Manage subscription appears after your first paid checkout — a Free account that has
        never checked out has nothing to manage.
      </p>

      <.docs_h2 id="payment-failure">If a payment fails</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        A failed renewal does not lock you out: Paddle retries the charge, and your plan
        and limits stay active while it retries.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Open <a
          href={~p"/app/billing"}
          class="font-medium text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >Settings → Billing</a>, choose <strong class="text-zinc-200">Manage subscription</strong>,
        and update the payment method — Paddle uses it for the next retry. To stop renewing
        instead, cancel in the Paddle portal. Every plan change is recorded in the <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/audit-and-siem"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >audit log</.link>.
      </p>

      <.docs_h2 id="retention">Plan changes and audit retention</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Each audit event gets a fixed retention deadline when it is written, so a plan change
        affects only later events: an upgrade keeps new history longer, and a downgrade shortens
        the window for new events without deleting older retained history. The windows are in the <a
          href="#plans"
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >table above</a>;
        retention behavior — pruning, the export API, and keeping history past
        the window in your SIEM — is in <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/audit-and-siem" <> "#retention"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >Audit &amp; SIEM</.link>.
      </p>
    </.docs_layout>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer />
</div>
